 "priv.short": "No login. No cookies. Results stay in your browser, unless you play in a room or a live game. Visits are counted without identifying anyone.",
 "priv.short_page": "No login. No cookies. Results stay in your browser, unless you play in a room or a live game.",
 "priv.long": "No login and no cookies. Your streak and your album are kept only in this browser.",
 "priv.world": "No login and no cookies.",
 "priv.duel": "No login and no cookies. A duel link carries only the day, the scores and the name the sender chose for themselves, inside the link itself: nothing reached a server, not even ours. The name you choose travels in every link you send. What your phone has merged is kept only in this browser.",
 "priv.rooms": "No login and no cookies. Outside your own browser, a room stores only this: each daily game a member finishes sends the game, the score, the day and their chosen name to the site's own small server, and nothing else — and nothing at all for anyone who is in no room. It keeps this month and the last, then deletes; a room nobody plays in for 60 days is deleted whole, and leaving a room deletes everything of yours at once.",
 "priv.group": "No login and no cookies. Your table's best result is kept only in this browser.",
 "priv.names": "No login and no cookies. The players' names and wins are forgotten when you leave this page.",
 "priv.table": "No login and no cookies. Your table's best journey is kept only in this browser; the players' names are forgotten when you leave this page.",
 "priv.live": "No login and no cookies. Live games: the name you type and your answers stay on Logicers' server for the game and are deleted a day after it ends (the server's own backups clear within 30 days). Nothing else about you is kept.",
 "priv.live_all": "No login and no cookies. Live games: the name you type and your answers stay on Logicers' server for the game and are deleted a day after it ends. Games people make: a saved game keeps only what its maker typed into it, with no name of the maker, and an email only as a one-way fingerprint, if the maker leaves one as a way back to a lost link (the address itself only if they also tick feedback emails, and only for those); it is deleted two months after its last use. Playing one alone keeps the name you type and your answers with the game, for its scoreboard, and they go when the game goes. A report keeps what its sender writes, the game's code, and a name and email only if given, for six months. The server's own backups clear within 30 days. Nothing else about you is kept.",
 "priv.counted_vp2": "Visits and plays are counted with GoatCounter, and visits also with Cloudflare Web Analytics, without identifying anyone.",
 "priv.counted_vp": "Visits and plays are counted with GoatCounter, without identifying anyone.",
 "priv.counted_v2": "Visits are counted with GoatCounter and Cloudflare Web Analytics, without identifying anyone.",
 "priv.counted_v": "Visits are counted with GoatCounter, without identifying anyone.",
 "priv.feedback": "If you choose to message Khayyam from the end-of-day card, what you write goes through Web3Forms, a form service, to Logicers' inbox, together with the day and the results of your games, and nothing else about you.",
 "priv.reminder": "If you turn on the daily reminder, Logicers' server keeps your browser's notification address, the hour you usually play, your time zone, your streak, the day you last played and your country until you turn it off (or a month and a half after your last visit), and sends at most one reminder a day.",
